+# SEMANTIC TRACE
+
+*trace-event* submits one bounded scope transition. Required options are
+*--id*, *--kind*, *--phase*, and *--status*. Optional *--parent* refers to an
+existing active scope; *--count* is a u16 decision count and *--uncertainty*
+is an integer from 0 to 1000. No application-supplied labels are accepted.
+
+Kinds: human, codex, fabric, jev, search, read, edit, tool, test, verify,
+worker, shell-command. Phases: start, update, finish. Statuses: active,
+passed, failed, cancelled. Start/update require active; finish requires a
+terminal status. Id and parent identity are immutable within retained history.
+
+*trace-reset* clears retained scope state. Both commands require an exact
+*--window-id* or ALACRITTY_WINDOW_ID and acknowledge validation failures.
+
